cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CommentInject, please cite it as below."
title: "CommentInject: A benchmark of adversarial code-comment injection against LLM vulnerability detectors"
type: dataset
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-01
authors:
  - family-names: Chokshi
    given-names: Sunny
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-4738-7759"
    affiliation: "University of the Cumberlands"
license: "MIT AND CC-BY-4.0"
keywords:
  - adversarial comment injection
  - prompt injection
  - vulnerability detection
  - large language models
  - code security
  - benchmark
abstract: >
  30 vulnerable Python functions across 14 CWE categories, 12 adversarial
  comment strategies in four families, and 3,360 recorded trials from four
  studies (attack ranking, comment-stripping defense, cross-model comparison,
  transferability) on four local code models.
